-- title:
--   Vélu function-field extension for an odd cyclic kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be an algebraically closed field, with no hypothesis on its characteristic, let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $F$ that is elliptic, let $Q$ be a point of the affine model of $W$ with $\operatorname{addOrderOf} Q = 2n+1$ for some $n \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $S = W.\mathrm{oddOrderSummingSet}\,Q\,n$ be the finite subset of $F \times F$ consisting of the coordinate pairs of $Q, 2Q, \dots, nQ$ (the pair $(0,0)$ standing for the point at infinity). Assume the Vélu quotient curve $W' = W.\mathrm{veluQuotient}\,S$, with coefficients $a_1, a_2, a_3, a_4 - 5\,T_S, a_6 - b_2 T_S - 7 W_S$, has $\Delta \ne 0$ and that its affine model is elliptic; assume further that each of $W$ and $W'$ carries a genus-one place gate, i.e. a bijection between its group of points and the set of places of its function field over $F$, all of degree $1$, which is centred in the sense that the classes of $X - x$ and $Y - y$ lie in the maximal ideal of the valuation subring attached to $(x,y)$, and that each satisfies the Abel property: a divisor of degree $0$ is principal precisely when its divisor sum vanishes. Then there exist an $F$-algebra homomorphism $\iota : F(W') \to F(W)$ between the function fields, a proof $h_\iota$ that $\iota$ is integral, and a proof $h_{\mathrm{fin}}$ that $F(W)$ is a finite module over $F(W')$ via $\iota$, such that: the rank $\mathrm{finrankAlong}\,F\,\iota$ of $F(W)$ over $F(W')$ is $2n+1$; for every witness of the pushforward norm formula along $\iota$, the induced additive map $W(F) \to W'(F)$ obtained from pushforward on $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ has kernel exactly $\langle Q \rangle = \mathrm{AddSubgroup.zmultiples}\,Q$; every $P \in \langle Q \rangle$ has $\mathrm{placeOfPoint}\,P$ restricting along $\iota$ (pullback of the valuation subring) to the place of the origin of $W'$; and for all $x, y \in F$ with $(x,y)$ a nonsingular point of $W$ not lying in $\langle Q \rangle$, the pair $(W.\mathrm{veluX}\,S\,x,\ W.\mathrm{veluY}\,S\,x\,y)$ is a nonsingular point of $W'$ and the place of $(x,y)$ restricts along $\iota$ to the place of that point.
--
--   This is the function-field form of Vélu's construction of the isogeny with kernel the cyclic group generated by a point of odd order, packaged as a finite integral extension $F(W') \subseteq F(W)$ of degree $2n+1$ whose place restriction is computed by Vélu's explicit coordinate formulas. It is the input to the construction of the point map of the Vélu isogeny and, through it, to the statements on full kernels of multiplication-by-$m$ and on the composite of two Vélu quotients.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_veluFunctionFieldHom_restrictAlong_placeOfPoint_eq_of_isAlgClosed.lean

